# 6. IDENTITY TRANSITION ENGINE

Use the browser View Transition API as progressive enhancement rather than building a fragile screenshot/WebGL replacement for the DOM.

`document.startViewTransition()` is now broadly available on current browser generations, but older browsers still require a normal state-change fallback.

Conceptually:

```ts
function switchIdentity(next: Identity) {
  const update = () => {
    document.documentElement.dataset.identity = next;
    setIdentity(next);
  };

  if (
    !document.startViewTransition ||
    prefersReducedMotion()
  ) {
    update();
    return;
  }

  document.startViewTransition(update);
}
```

Target:

```text
~400–700 ms
```

for the complete identity choreography.

Not every element should animate.

The X, hero typography, key imagery, navigation and background atmosphere may transform.

Body copy should generally remain stable.

Reduced-motion mode should become an immediate or subtle crossfade.

The goal is:

**continuity without spectacle fatigue.**

