# 7. DESIGN TOKEN ENGINE

Use [Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/docs/theme?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_x-social-details_comments-action_comment-text&utm_source=chatgpt.com) v4 as a utility compiler over a semantic CSS token architecture.

Tailwind v4's `@theme` variables generate utilities and CSS variables.

The important separation is:

```text
PRIMITIVE TOKENS
↓
SEMANTIC TOKENS
↓
IDENTITY RESOLUTION
↓
APPEARANCE RESOLUTION
↓
COMPONENT TOKENS
```

Example:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  --color-surface: var(--sx-surface);
  --color-surface-elevated: var(--sx-surface-elevated);
  --color-text-primary: var(--sx-text-primary);
  --color-text-secondary: var(--sx-text-secondary);
  --color-accent: var(--sx-accent);
  --color-border: var(--sx-border);

  --font-display: var(--sx-font-display);
  --font-body: var(--sx-font-body);
}
```

Then:

```css
:root[data-identity="karim"] {
  --sx-font-display: var(--font-karim-display);
  --sx-font-body: var(--font-karim-body);
  --sx-motion-factor: .7;
}

:root[data-identity="saint"] {
  --sx-font-display: var(--font-saint-display);
  --sx-font-body: var(--font-saint-body);
  --sx-motion-factor: 1;
}
```

Appearance resolves independently.

```css
:root[data-theme="light"] {
  color-scheme: light;

  --sx-surface: #ffffff;
  --sx-surface-elevated: #f6f7f9;
  --sx-text-primary: #101114;
  --sx-text-secondary: #60646c;
}

:root[data-theme="dark"] {
  color-scheme: dark;

  --sx-surface: #050507;
  --sx-surface-elevated: #0c0c11;
  --sx-text-primary: #f7f7f8;
  --sx-text-secondary: #a1a1aa;
}
```

Then identity adds character.

```css
:root[data-identity="karim"] {
  --sx-accent: #2563eb;
}

:root[data-identity="saint"] {
  --sx-accent: #d946ef;
  --sx-glow: rgba(217, 70, 239, .35);
}
```

CSS variable changes avoid React component remounting, but they do **not** mean rendering is free. Changes may cause style recalculation, painting or compositing.

That distinction matters.

