# 18. VIDEO PIPELINE

Use [Mux](https://www.mux.com/docs/guides/stream-videos-in-4k?utm_source=chatgpt.com) as the baseline managed video platform.

Pipeline:

```text
SOURCE VIDEO
     │
     ▼
R2 MASTER ARCHIVE
     │
     ├───────────────┐
     │               │
     ▼               ▼
MEDIA METADATA     MUX INGEST
                     │
                     ▼
                  PROCESS
                     │
          ┌──────────┼───────────┐
          ▼          ▼           ▼
        HLS      THUMBNAILS   CAPTIONS
          │          │           │
          └──────────┼───────────┘
                     ▼
                 WEBHOOK
                     │
                     ▼
                 POSTGRES
                     │
                     ▼
            SAINTXVERSE PLAYER
```

Mux currently supports on-demand 4K/2160p when `max_resolution_tier: "2160p"` is configured. Its live output remains capped at 1080p even if higher-resolution input is accepted.

Do not force 4K.

Default:

```text
AUTO
```

Optional preference:

```text
Auto
Data Saver
720p
1080p
1440p
2160p
```

The ABR system should choose the actual rendition.

Mux supports resolution caps on playback URLs, while the default manifest allows the player to choose based on conditions.

