# 24. SPOTIFY POLICY

[Spotify Web Playback SDK](https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-playback-sdk?utm_source=chatgpt.com) can provide browser playback, but it should **not** be treated as a universally available SaintxVerse playback backend.

Current official documentation says Web Playback requires a Spotify Premium access token and explicitly states that commercial streaming integrations require Spotify approval. Spotify also prohibits synchronizing Spotify recordings with visual media through its platform.

Therefore:

```text
Spotify track
     │
     ├── metadata / attribution
     ├── Open in Spotify
     └── optional approved playback integration
```

Never:

```text
Spotify audio
→ extract PCM
→ run Saint visualizer
→ rebroadcast
```

Also, Spotify Audio Features and Audio Analysis were removed from new Web API use cases in November 2024.

Therefore SaintxVerse should compute its own analysis from Saint-owned masters.

---

# 25. YOUTUBE POLICY

Use the official [YouTube IFrame Player API](https://developers.google.com/youtube/iframe_api_reference?utm_source=chatgpt.com).

Do not use:

```text
0×0 YouTube player
hidden iframe
player underneath custom artwork
overlay covering YouTube controls
audio extraction
YouTube-as-CDN
```

YouTube currently requires embedded players to have a viewport of at least 200×200 pixels and explicitly prohibits overlays that obscure any part of the embedded player.

Premium integration therefore means:

```text
SaintxVerse cinematic frame
        │
        └── visible compliant YouTube player
```

rather than disguising YouTube playback as native playback.

