# 46. PHASER LIFECYCLE

Load Phaser only when necessary.

Phaser's own `Game.destroy(removeCanvas, noReturn)` is asynchronous: destruction is flagged for the next frame. Its documentation also states that `noReturn=true` frees core plugin memory when Phaser will not be used again on the page.

Therefore the default lifecycle should be:

```text
create game
↓
attach Phaser listeners
↓
run
↓
remove custom listeners/workers/audio
↓
game.destroy(true, appropriateNoReturn)
↓
wait for destroy event where necessary
↓
release references
```

Do **not** make manual `WEBGL_lose_context` calls the default teardown strategy.

Phaser should own its renderer lifecycle.

Manual forced context loss is an escape hatch for diagnosed browser/resource problems, not normal cleanup.

Also clean:

```text
workers
AudioContexts
AudioWorklets
ResizeObservers
MutationObservers
timers
window listeners
document listeners
custom sockets
custom textures
external caches
```

Lazy loading reduces initial cost.

It does not mean "zero RAM impact."

